t recreated the old Sega games but  it's actually turned them into what you  wanted them to be as a child they've  created a much more detailed world and I  think it just looks fantastic  in her whole commute that glides through  the air in your task is go through 17  different areas and find a way of  freeing your other snake friends it's a  bit of a confusing game but it looks  absolutely incredible the gorgeous kind  of psychedelic colors with the alien  like flora and fauna the way that you  interact with the environment is  incredibly creative as always with games  like this it's strong points are also a  little bit of a negative it can be very  confusing because it doesn't have any of  the clutter of a usual game there's no  Maps there's no counting it doesn't tell  you what you've done although it makes  the game look great it means that you do  often find yourself lost in the war in  like endless areas that there seem to be  however I do really enjoy the fact that  it doesn't take you for a tutorial  kicking and screaming and just lets you  explore and find the world in your own  way this gave vs. a sandbox game in  which you plays a prisoner and your role  is to break out the prison now it's a  time management game so you've got to  try and find a way of breaking out of  the prison while sticking to the strict  schedule you don't want to draw  attention to yourself by not turning up  for roll call but you've also got to  figure a way out and it's really clever  in the way that there are so many ways  you can break out the prison you can do  a classic great escape you can dig a  hole or you can disguise yourself as a  prison officer or cause a rise and try  and sneak out it's really amazing how  much they've managed to fit into this  little game the classic 8-bit graphics  look fantastic although the controls can  be a bit fiddly it's a little bit  difficult to master them and it takes a  little bit of time to learn that as I  did the dimmer screen punching 